            <ArticleTitle>Angiographic evidence of myocardial channels after percutaneous transmyocardial laser treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>532-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The available clinical reports on percutaneous transmyocardial laser revascularization do not provide data on the visibility of the channels after the procedures. We present the case of a patient who had clear angiographic evidence of the presence of myocardial channels immediately after percutaneous transmyocardial laser revascularization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
